  "donor_comparison": "Pinned reconstructed low cases cap/raise via u32 comparisons, matching encoded unsigned HI. High case chooses the low bound by unsigned comparison, then handles zero, negative, and otherwise signed system-stack sizes, consistent with encoded EQ/LT/GE. Donor low ID1 hardcodes 027fafcc; JUS literal is 027f9c08. Pinned memory constants derive 027ff000 and0380ff80. These corroborate a hypothesis, not JUS names/types/ownership.",
  "condition_semantics": "HI uses C=1,Z=0 (unsigned higher); EQ uses Z=1; LT uses N!=V; GE uses N=V. Conditional arithmetic keeps its condition despite an always-fallthrough transfer; BXEQ retains passed unknown target and failed selected continuation. No runtime feasibility or return inference.",
